840
00:35:19.620 --> 00:35:22.800
and YouTubers struggling with mental health

841
00:35:22.800 --> 00:35:25.410
and all those issues because I couldn't imagine

842
00:35:25.410 --> 00:35:27.960
being an 18, 19-year old girl

843
00:35:27.960 --> 00:35:29.790
who found a similar level of success

844
00:35:29.790 --> 00:35:31.740
and she felt that obligation.
Right.

845
00:35:32.730 --> 00:35:34.260
I have friends of mine who are that age,

846
00:35:34.260 --> 00:35:37.110
24-year old dude who just like put everything he had

847
00:35:37.110 --> 00:35:41.100
into his videos and then a year later, he's just toast.

848
00:35:41.100 --> 00:35:42.720
So that was really challenging

849
00:35:42.720 --> 00:35:44.343
and it made me really vulnerable in a way

850
00:35:44.343 --> 00:35:45.990
that I never wanna do that again.

851
00:35:45.990 --> 00:35:46.823
Yeah.

852
00:35:48.240 --> 00:35:51.840
I just can't imagine the toil and the toll

853
00:35:51.840 --> 00:35:53.820
that that would've taken.

854
00:35:53.820 --> 00:35:57.750
But what is interesting to me in reflecting back on it is,

855
00:35:57.750 --> 00:36:00.510
at that moment in time, certainly, vlogging wasn't new.

856
00:36:00.510 --> 00:36:01.920
There were plenty of people vlogging,

857
00:36:01.920 --> 00:36:05.220
