867
00:36:31.800 --> 00:36:35.250
Like every story did have this react structure,

868
00:36:35.250 --> 00:36:36.930
a very traditional structure.

869
00:36:36.930 --> 00:36:38.520
And even if that story was very small,

870
00:36:38.520 --> 00:36:42.060
like I need to retrieve my drone or something like that,

871
00:36:42.060 --> 00:36:46.080
you would make it interesting through specificity

872
00:36:46.080 --> 00:36:50.010
and this economy that you applied to storytelling,

873
00:36:50.010 --> 00:36:53.070
to just showing what is meaningful

874
00:36:53.070 --> 00:36:54.630
to propel the story forward.

875
00:36:54.630 --> 00:36:58.110
And I think that's what people connected with,

876
00:36:58.110 --> 00:36:59.520
even if they weren't aware of it.

877
00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:00.353
Like they think

878
00:37:00.353 --> 00:37:02.070
it's because you have these fancy drone shots

879
00:37:02.070 --> 00:37:02.903
and stuff like that.

880
00:37:02.903 --> 00:37:05.550
But really, the engine behind the whole thing

881
00:37:05.550 --> 00:37:07.230
was the storytelling.

882
00:37:07.230 --> 00:37:09.270
Yeah, and I think also, thank you for saying that.

883
00:37:09.270 --> 00:37:11.400
I think that what you just articulated

884
00:37:11.400 --> 00:37:13.680
is a much harder thing to define.

885
00:37:13.680 --> 00:37:16.107
It's really easy to be like, oh, I love the way you shoot it

886
00:37:16.107 --> 00:37:18.120
and your music's so cool.

887
00:37:18.120 --> 00:37:21.030
The irony is like you just type Casey music into YouTube,

888
00:37:21.030 --> 00:37:23.483
you can just download all the same shit that I use.

889
00:37:24.420 --> 00:37:25.380
That's really easy to define.

890
00:37:25.380 --> 00:37:27.870
It's really hard to define what you just said,

891
00:37:27.870 --> 00:37:30.420
but I think you, that was certainly my pursuit.

892
00:37:30.420 --> 00:37:32.712
Like I remember for example like,

