01:04:16.500 --> 01:04:20.820
which is that like sensationalism equals views.

1532
01:04:20.820 --> 01:04:23.220
And that endless pursuit, you get the views,

1533
01:04:23.220 --> 01:04:25.380
sensationalism gives you views, some more sensationalism,

1534
01:04:25.380 --> 01:04:28.710
some more views, and you just keep chasing that tail

1535
01:04:28.710 --> 01:04:33.710
until something extraordinary happens that's not good.

1536
01:04:34.440 --> 01:04:36.270
And you think about Logan Paul

1537
01:04:36.270 --> 01:04:38.130
and what happened to him early in his career,

1538
01:04:38.130 --> 01:04:40.290
which was just completely torpedoed

1539
01:04:40.290 --> 01:04:43.050
by his own shitty judgment and it forced him

1540
01:04:43.050 --> 01:04:45.213
to completely reinvent who he was.

1541
01:04:46.170 --> 01:04:48.660
And there's a dozen other creators that have reached

1542
01:04:48.660 --> 01:04:50.790
that sort of global superstardom level

1543
01:04:50.790 --> 01:04:53.430
that have then sidelined their own careers

1544
01:04:53.430 --> 01:04:55.860
because they're chasing after something

1545
01:04:55.860 --> 01:04:59.730
that is dangerous, exploitive, stupid, harmful

1546
01:04:59.730 --> 01:05:02.040
in something atrocious comes from it

1547
01:05:02.040 --> 01:05:03.270
and it ends their career.

1548
01:05:03.270 --> 01:05:05.397
And that's exactly what happened to him.

1549
01:05:05.397 --> 01:05:07.410
And I think it's whether,

1550
01:05:07.410 --> 01:05:09.510
or talking about one of his closest friends

1551
01:05:09.510 --> 01:05:14.350
being horribly injured, almost killed in pursuit of a stunt

1552
01:05:15.330 --> 01:05:18.210
or a young woman being victimized

1553
01:05:18.210 --> 01:05:20.640
in pursuit of a funny scene.

1554
01:05:20.640 --> 01:05:22.590
It's all part of a much bigger discussion,

1555
01:05:22.590 --> 01:05:25.503
which is like, where does accountability lie?

1556
01:05:26.730 --> 01:05:28.530
Certainly, it lies with the creator.

1557
01:05:29.460 --> 01:05:33.930
And I think David does, I think he does a pretty fair job

1558
01:05:33.930 --> 01:05:35.400
in the movie of kind of owning that.

1559
01:05:35.400 --> 01:05:37.710
And you know-
Does he own that?

1560
01:05:37.710 --> 01:05:39.000
'cause my sense was that,

1561
01:05:39.000 --> 01:05:41.670
there is a sort of lack of self-awareness.

1562
01:05:41.670 --> 01:05:43.170
There's certainly a lack of self-awareness.

1563
01:05:43.170 --> 01:05:46.323
Really crock the severity of the situation.

1564
01:05:47.580 --> 01:05:48.630
Absolutely, there is.

1565
01:05:48.630 --> 01:05:51.240
And I think that those sorts of things take time

1566
01:05:51.240 --> 01:05:53.220
and without defending him,

1567
01:05:53.220 --> 01:05:55.170
I think that those sorts of things say, take time.

1568
01:05:55.170 --> 01:05:57.480
But I do know him and I know his character.

1569
01:05:57.480 --> 01:05:59.190
He's not an apathetic person.

1570
01:05:59.190 --> 01:06:01.470
But I think you raise to a place of wanting

1571
01:06:01.470 --> 01:06:03.480
to defend yourself when things like this happen.

1572
01:06:03.480 --> 01:06:05.460
And that can come across as a lack of self awareness

1573
01:06:05.460 --> 01:06:06.293
or understanding.

1574
01:06:06.293 --> 01:06:09.900
But you know, there's a back and forth he and I have

1575
01:06:09.900 --> 01:06:12.183
in the movie where I say like,

1576
01:06:13.170 --> 01:06:16.110
understanding you didn't know what had transpired that night

1577
01:06:16.110 --> 01:06:17.670
that this young woman was assaulted.

1578
01:06:17.670 --> 01:06:20.700
But looking back at it now, you still like,

1579
01:06:20.700 --> 01:06:25.230
let this guy who had a history of abuse leverage a fame

1580
01:06:25.230 --> 01:06:26.850
and an influence that you had created

1581
01:06:26.850 --> 01:06:30.231
to attract these young girls to try to connect with them

1582
01:06:30.231 --> 01:06:34.740
in a way that was obviously predicated on something sexual.

1583
01:06:34.740 --> 01:06:36.930
And I was like, don't you see

1584
01:06:36.930 --> 01:06:40.350
that that's grossly inappropriate?

1585
01:06:40.350 --> 01:06:43.230
And he says very honestly, like, I didn't see it then,

1586
01:06:43.230 --> 01:06:46.480
but of course, I see it now, it's fucking disgusting. And-

1587
01:06:46.480 --> 01:06:48.450
Yeah, it doesn't have to be intentional,

1588
01:06:48.450 --> 01:06:52.560
but it's so severely kind of nonchalant

1589
01:06:52.560 --> 01:06:54.840
about the whole thing.
Absolutely-

1590
01:06:54.840 --> 01:06:56.490
And you have these powerful incentives

1591
01:06:56.490 --> 01:06:58.980
that are driving you towards that place of more

1592
01:06:58.980 --> 01:07:01.020
and more and more, crazier, crazier, crazier.

1593
01:07:01.020 --> 01:07:03.330
And his whole thing was like,

1594
01:07:03.330 --> 01:07:05.850
each stunt would be more outrageous than the one prior.

1595
01:07:05.850 --> 01:07:09.390
I mean, it is qualitatively different in some sense

1596
01:07:09.390 --> 01:07:10.380
from what you were doing,

1597
01:07:10.380 --> 01:07:13.020
which is kind of these mini stories every day.

1598
01:07:13.020 --> 01:07:17.250
It wasn't about doing extreme things like that would-

1599
01:07:17.250 --> 01:07:19.291
Well, I mean the only thing like he and I had in common

1600
01:07:19.291 --> 01:07:20.670
is that we both put videos on YouTube.

1601
01:07:20.670 --> 01:07:24.300
Yeah.
But, you know,

1602
01:07:24.300 --> 01:07:27.420
at the end of it all, and I say this without absolving him

1603
01:07:27.420 --> 01:07:29.640
or any other creative of their wrong,

1604
01:07:29.640 --> 01:07:32.970
who's had a downfall like he had of their wrongdoing.

1605
01:07:32.970 --> 01:07:36.300
But you know, he is obviously the story,

1606
01:07:36.300 --> 01:07:39.750
but I presented him more as a case study.

1607
01:07:39.750 --> 01:07:40.583
And I think a lot

1608
01:07:40.583 --> 01:07:44.220
of the more established traditional media reviews

1609
01:07:44.220 --> 01:07:45.960
of the movie that came out of its premiere

1610
01:07:45.960 --> 01:07:49.200
in South by Southwest got that very much so.

1611
01:07:49.200 --> 01:07:50.193
Which is that like-

1612
01:07:51.240 --> 01:07:53.640
There will be another, this will happen again and again.

1613
01:07:53.640 --> 01:07:56.880
Sure, but also before he was, you know,

1614
01:07:56.880 --> 01:07:58.590
before he was canceled,

1615
01:07:58.590 --> 01:08:00.450
before he had every contract that he had

1616
01:08:00.450 --> 01:08:03.060
with every brand canceled and before YouTube cut him off

1617
01:08:03.060 --> 01:08:07.440
and before he faced all these very severe consequences.

1618
01:08:07.440 --> 01:08:10.830
Before that, he had 7 billion views, 7 billion.

1619
01:08:10.830 --> 01:08:13.050
That's more views than every Super Bowl

1620
01:08:13.050 --> 01:08:14.610
since the inception of the Super Bowl

1621
01:08:14.610 --> 01:08:18.360
until this year combined, 7 billion views.

1622
01:08:18.360 --> 01:08:22.320
So 7 billion views saying to him, good job, man.

1623
01:08:22.320 --> 01:08:24.720
Here's the money, keep going, we wanna see more.

1624
01:08:24.720 --> 01:08:26.340
Here's the thumbs up, we love you.

1625
01:08:26.340 --> 01:08:28.407
And the money's crazy.
And the money's crazy.

1626
01:08:28.407 --> 01:08:30.390
And these are young people.
They're young people.

1627
01:08:30.390 --> 01:08:32.640
They're zero oversight or regulation.

1628
01:08:32.640 --> 01:08:35.460
I know you're friends with Steve-O, you know,

1629
01:08:35.460 --> 01:08:39.485
the obvious analogy is to something like Jackass,

1630
01:08:39.485 --> 01:08:42.588
they go into those stunts, you know this,

1631
01:08:42.588 --> 01:08:44.430
they've figured it all out.

1632
01:08:44.430 --> 01:08:47.400
They have safety protocols and measures in place.

1633
01:08:47.400 --> 01:08:48.720
Like it's a very different piece.

1634
01:08:48.720 --> 01:08:51.277
I think Jackass is a very, very good example

1635
01:08:51.277 --> 01:08:52.680
of how you're supposed to do that,

1636
01:08:52.680 --> 01:08:55.020
which is Jackass is,

1637
01:08:55.020 --> 01:08:57.660
every member of Jackass that's on camera

1638
01:08:57.660 --> 01:09:02.660
is they're under entirely, contractually, consensual terms.

1639
01:09:04.260 --> 01:09:07.170
Everyone there knows exactly what they have to gain

1640
01:09:07.170 --> 01:09:08.513
and what the price is for that.

1641
01:09:08.513 --> 01:09:12.210
Like it is well defined on Jackass,

1642
01:09:12.210 --> 01:09:13.860
the lack of power dynamic.

1643
01:09:13.860 --> 01:09:15.885
There is no power dynamic on Jackass.

1644
01:09:15.885 --> 01:09:17.430
This is what we're doing,

1645
01:09:17.430 --> 01:09:19.530
are you part of this or are you not?

1646
01:09:19.530 --> 01:09:20.363
And if you're part of this,

1647
01:09:20.363 --> 01:09:22.080
you know what you're signing up for.

1648
01:09:22.080 --> 01:09:23.550
And I think in the creator space,

1649
01:09:23.550 --> 01:09:25.350
it's an antithetical to that.

1650
01:09:25.350 --> 01:09:26.760
No one knows,

1651
01:09:26.760 --> 01:09:29.010
you're just a kid walking around the video camera

1652
01:09:29.010 --> 01:09:31.560
trying to capture moments of sensationalism

1653
01:09:31.560 --> 01:09:33.960
or create moments of sensationalism.

1654
01:09:33.960 --> 01:09:35.460
And if you're on the other side of that and you're like,

1655
01:09:35.460 --> 01:09:39.090
shit, I'll do anything for fame, well, what does that mean?

1656
01:09:39.090 --> 01:09:40.770
And where can that lead?

1657
01:09:40.770 --> 01:09:43.170
And that can lead to really devastating places.

1658
01:09:43.170 --> 01:09:44.160
And I think that this

1659
01:09:44.160 --> 01:09:47.910
is a very challenging discussion to have

1660
01:09:47.910 --> 01:09:49.380
because it's so nuanced.

1661
01:09:49.380 --> 01:09:54.380
I think what is very easy is to point to specific outcomes

1662
01:09:54.540 --> 01:09:58.110
and specific happenstance and say, well, that was fucked up.

1663
01:09:58.110 --> 01:10:00.570
He's stupid, he should have never done that.

1664
01:10:00.570 --> 01:10:02.010
You know, Logan should have never walked

1665
01:10:02.010 --> 01:10:05.340
into that forest in Japan.

1666
01:10:05.340 --> 01:10:06.780
And it's like, sure, but what about the day

1667
01:10:06.780 --> 01:10:09.150
before he did that when he was celebrated

1668
01:10:09.150 --> 01:10:12.030
for doing very similar shit for years.

1669
01:10:12.030 --> 01:10:14.670
Right, so it's less about pointing fingers at individuals

1670
01:10:14.670 --> 01:10:19.670
and more about illuminating these problematic aspects of-

1671
01:10:19.920 --> 01:10:22.650
With the big asterisk, which is again-

1672
01:10:22.650 --> 01:10:24.511
As somebody who's benefited tremendously-

1673
01:10:24.511 --> 01:10:25.762
No, that's not the asterisk.

1674
01:10:25.762 --> 01:10:27.300
The asterisk is that like,

1675
01:10:27.300 --> 01:10:30.300
I don't wanna defend these individuals

1676
01:10:30.300 --> 01:10:32.280
that have done fucked up shit on these platforms.

1677
01:10:32.280 --> 01:10:33.879
Like the ownership is theirs.

1678
01:10:33.879 --> 01:10:36.330
They need to own that

1679
01:10:36.330 --> 01:10:38.190
in whatever consequences they might face.

1680
01:10:38.190 --> 01:10:40.080
And that's certainly the case in my documentary

1681
01:10:40.080 --> 01:10:42.270
is I don't absolve him of any of his wrongdoing

1682
01:10:42.270 --> 01:10:44.070
or any of his poor judgment.

1683
01:10:44.070 --> 01:10:46.290
But I think you can have both of these discussions.

1684
01:10:46.290 --> 01:10:49.080
I think that it's very necessary to examine what happened

1685
01:10:49.080 --> 01:10:53.730
in this one person's career that led to such turmoil,

1686
01:10:53.730 --> 01:10:56.243
but also asking why did that happen?

1687
01:10:56.243 --> 01:10:58.530
Like in what world has that been enabled?

1688
01:10:58.530 --> 01:11:01.593
I think it's a very fair, much harder question.

1689
01:11:02.670 --> 01:11:04.740
And I hope that that my documentary

1690
01:11:04.740 --> 01:11:05.910
is able to sort of elevate that.

1691
01:11:05.910 --> 01:11:08.820
Yeah, what's interesting, and I say this as somebody

1692
01:11:08.820 --> 01:11:10.260
who hasn't seen the movie,

1693
01:11:10.260 --> 01:11:12.880
but my sense is that you got involved in it

1694
01:11:14.321 --> 01:11:15.154
'cause you followed him around,

1695
01:11:15.154 --> 01:11:17.190
you followed David around for a couple years, right?

1696
01:11:17.190 --> 01:11:21.270
So when you first began that journey,

1697
01:11:21.270 --> 01:11:23.070
it was more about like,

1698
01:11:23.070 --> 01:11:26.190
this is the next generation of creators.

1699
01:11:26.190 --> 01:11:29.250
And I wanna kind of tell the story

1700
01:11:29.250 --> 01:11:33.240
of what the behind the scenes of this is really like,

1701
01:11:33.240 --> 01:11:34.770
like how does this actually function

1702
01:11:34.770 --> 01:11:38.113
and then it became something else entirely.

1703
01:11:38.113 --> 01:11:41.730
I loved David, like I still have a tremendous fondness

1704
01:11:41.730 --> 01:11:43.290
for him, even though this movie

1705
01:11:43.290 --> 01:11:45.663
is very critical of his actions.

1706
01:11:46.500 --> 01:11:47.970
So much so that it's,

1707
01:11:47.970 --> 01:11:51.420
he and I no longer have a friendship because of this movie,

1708
01:11:51.420 --> 01:11:54.270
but I had a tremendous fondness for him,

1709
01:11:54.270 --> 01:11:56.250
both personally and professionally.

1710
01:11:56.250 --> 01:11:59.580
His videos were really funny and I was part of that audience

1711
01:11:59.580 --> 01:12:01.080
that was able to sort of turn to blind eye

1712
01:12:01.080 --> 01:12:02.910
to the more questionable moments in the video

1713
01:12:02.910 --> 01:12:05.010
because you assume what you're seeing

1714
01:12:05.010 --> 01:12:06.780
is entirely consensual.

1715
01:12:06.780 --> 01:12:11.310
And I saw in him a superstar before he was successful,

1716
01:12:11.310 --> 01:12:14.760
I said, this kid's going to fucking explode, and he did.

1717
01:12:14.760 --> 01:12:16.770
And that was the story that I wanted to tell,

1718
01:12:16.770 --> 01:12:21.210
my own experience on YouTube was so unbelievably unexpected

1719
01:12:21.210 --> 01:12:23.790
and overwhelming that I wanted to tell that story.

1720
01:12:23.790 --> 01:12:26.100
But I needed somebody else to tell it through

1721
01:12:26.100 --> 01:12:28.500
that was more interesting and better looking than me.

1722
01:12:28.500 --> 01:12:31.410
And David was that character, and yeah, look,

1723
01:12:31.410 --> 01:12:34.710
I spent two hours interviewing his high school teachers.

1724
01:12:34.710 --> 01:12:36.450
And I went back to his high school in Chicago

1725
01:12:36.450 --> 01:12:39.360
and met with his tennis coach and I interviewed his parents

1726
01:12:39.360 --> 01:12:41.010
and I hired a Hungarian translator

1727
01:12:41.010 --> 01:12:43.683
so I could interview his grandmother in Slovakia.

1728
01:12:44.520 --> 01:12:45.353
Wow.

1729
01:12:45.353 --> 01:12:46.186
And none of that's in the movie.

1730
01:12:46.186 --> 01:12:47.019
That's not the movie at all.

1731
01:12:47.019 --> 01:12:49.860
The movie's about this one night.

1732
01:12:49.860 --> 01:12:51.534
And what that means, because I think that

1733
01:12:51.534 --> 01:12:55.680
if I was sort of forced to confront an intellectual honesty,

1734
01:12:55.680 --> 01:12:57.180
which is, what is this movie?

1735
01:12:57.180 --> 01:12:59.400
And can you tell the story about

1736
01:12:59.400 --> 01:13:00.960
what his high school years were like

1737
01:13:00.960 --> 01:13:04.170
without it feeling like you're trying to make him

1738
01:13:04.170 --> 01:13:05.700
a more empathetic character?

1739
01:13:05.700 --> 01:13:08.610
When really like this was about this one night.

1740
01:13:08.610 --> 01:13:09.443
And there were a lot

1741
01:13:09.443 --> 01:13:12.540
of those very challenging narrative considerations

1742
01:13:12.540 --> 01:13:14.940
that I had to make as a filmmaker

1743
01:13:14.940 --> 01:13:17.520
before I could make them as a friend.

1744
01:13:17.520 --> 01:13:20.160
I think that the latter was irrelevant.

1745
01:13:20.160 --> 01:13:22.350
The fact that he was my friend became irrelevant

1746
01:13:22.350 --> 01:13:26.130
if I was gonna have any integrity behind the movie.

1747
01:13:26.130 --> 01:13:29.160
And the integrity of the movie ultimately

1748
01:13:29.160 --> 01:13:31.500
required a fracture in the relationship, right?

1749
01:13:31.500 --> 01:13:33.360
Like, he hasn't spoken to you.

1750
01:13:33.360 --> 01:13:34.193
I mean, I don't-

1751
01:13:34.193 --> 01:13:36.243
Has he seen the movie?
Yeah, of course.

1752
01:13:37.185 --> 01:13:38.018
He hates it.

1753
01:13:38.018 --> 01:13:39.883
But I don't think that, at the end of the day,

1754
01:13:39.883 --> 01:13:41.520
I have to live with myself

1755
01:13:41.520 --> 01:13:46.520
and integrity is a interesting word because it's like,

1756
01:13:48.540 --> 01:13:51.090
what about your integrity as a friend to David?

1757
01:13:51.090 --> 01:13:55.080
And I think that's really hard thing for me to confront,

1758
01:13:55.080 --> 01:13:57.510
but you know, I come back to this place of like,

1759
01:13:57.510 --> 01:14:00.003
this was not what I signed up for.

1760
01:14:01.050 --> 01:14:02.433
He said those words to me

1761
01:14:02.433 --> 01:14:04.320
and I think it's very fair for me to say those words back.

1762
01:14:04.320 --> 01:14:06.510
Like, this is not what I signed up for.

1763
01:14:06.510 --> 01:14:08.940
Meaning, when he agreed to be filmed by you.

1764
01:14:08.940 --> 01:14:09.773
Yeah.
Yeah.

1765
01:14:10.830 --> 01:14:11.820
And when I agreed,

1766
01:14:11.820 --> 01:14:14.040
when I decided to make a movie about him,

1767
01:14:14.040 --> 01:14:16.590
you know, he's so psyched to make a movie

1768
01:14:16.590 --> 01:14:19.770
when it's about his tennis coach in Chicago.

1769
01:14:19.770 --> 01:14:24.120
And, you know, him selling out huge spaces

1770
01:14:24.120 --> 01:14:26.760
to give talks to high school kids and college kids.

1771
01:14:26.760 --> 01:14:29.280
Like that's really fun and exciting.

1772
01:14:29.280 --> 01:14:31.290
But then it came about something much darker

1773
01:14:31.290 --> 01:14:33.570
and at the end of the day, I thought all I could do,

1774
01:14:33.570 --> 01:14:38.570
both for my own sense of responsibility and humanity

1775
01:14:38.610 --> 01:14:42.783
was do everything I could to let him speak for himself.

1776
01:14:44.130 --> 01:14:46.290
And speak truth to what happened.

1777
01:14:46.290 --> 01:14:48.810
And I think I gave him every opportunity

1778
01:14:48.810 --> 01:14:49.767
in the world to do that.

1779
01:14:49.767 --> 01:14:52.590
And I did my very best to make that abundantly clear

1780
01:14:52.590 --> 01:14:55.260
in the movie, I'm not in the movie at all.

1781
01:14:55.260 --> 01:14:57.630
It's a very traditional documentary.

1782
01:14:57.630 --> 01:15:00.780
But he seemed like he's still doing his thing. Right?

1783
01:15:00.780 --> 01:15:03.924
